Only clean, finalized notebooks

learning path
Layer 0: Foundations (Week 1–2)
- Probability refresher: random variables, expectation, conditional expectation, filtrations, martingales
- Brownian Motion — definition, properties, quadratic variation
- Itô Calculus — Itô integral, Itô's lemma, SDEs
- Risk-Neutral vs Real-World Measure — Girsanov's theorem, equivalent martingale measures

Layer 1: Classical Pricing (Week 2–3)
- Option Payoffs — calls, puts, spreads, digitals, path-dependent
- Black-Scholes Model & Greeks — derivation via replication, delta, gamma, vega, theta
- Monte Carlo Estimation — law of large numbers, CLT, variance reduction, discretization bias

Layer 2: Numerical Methods for SDEs (Week 3–4)
- Euler-Maruyama Discretization — convergence, bias-variance tradeoff
- Heston Model — the SDE system, Feller condition, implied volatility smile
- Broadie-Kaya Scheme — exact simulation of Heston (CIR process + stock)

Layer 3: Risk Measures and Pricing (Week 4–5)
- Convex Risk Measures — axioms (monotonicity, convexity, cash-invariance), coherent vs convex
- Rockafellar-Uryasev CVaR Formula — the optimization representation of CVaR
- The Indifference Price 

Layer 4: Deep Hedging (Week 5–6)
- Deep Hedging framework — Buehler et al., Sections 2–4
- Neural network architectures — feedforward, recurrent, semi-recurrent
- Training via SGD/Adam — loss functions, backpropagation, minibatches

Layer 5: JEPA (Week 6–8)
- Self-supervised learning — contrastive vs predictive, representation learning
- JEPA — joint embedding, predictor, target encoder, stop-gradient
- I-JEPA / V-JEPA / TD-JEPA — instantiations
- FinJEPA — closest existing work to your thesis